<PageTitle>TextBox SDK</PageTitle>

<h1 class="text-2xl font-bold">.NET SDK</h1>
<p class="opacity-70">Typed client for the mock SMS API — <code>TextBox.Sdk</code> (<code>netstandard2.0</code>, NSwag-generated).</p>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6">Install</h2>
<pre class="bg-base-200 rounded-box p-3 text-sm overflow-x-auto">dotnet add package TextBox.Sdk</pre>
<p class="text-sm opacity-60 mt-2">Available on <a href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/TextBox.Sdk" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link">nuget.org</a>.</p>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6">Use (no DI required)</h2>
<pre class="bg-base-200 rounded-box p-3 text-sm overflow-x-auto">var client = new TextBoxClient(new TextBoxOptions
{
    BaseAddress = "http://localhost:8080",
    ApiKey = "secret-1", // optional: omit when the API is open
});

var sent = await client.SendAsync(
    SendSmsRequest.Create("+123", "hello"));
var inbox = await client.ListAsync();
var one = await client.GetAsync(sent.Id);
await client.ClearAsync();</pre>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6">Use (Microsoft DI, optional)</h2>
<pre class="bg-base-200 rounded-box p-3 text-sm overflow-x-auto">services.AddTextBoxClient(
    "http://localhost:8080", apiKey: "secret-1");</pre>

<h2 class="text-lg font-semibold mt-6">API key behavior</h2>
<p class="text-sm opacity-80"><code>POST /api/messages</code> requires the key only when the server has one configured — reads never do. The client sends <code>Authorization: Bearer &lt;key&gt;</code> only when <code>ApiKey</code> is set, so one build works against both open and secured mocks. Without a valid key the API returns <code>401 {"error":"Missing or invalid API key."}</code> (surfaced as <code>TextBoxApiException</code>).</p>

